course: dictionary
lesson: 6784
title: Orange: a fruit and a colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Orange is a good example. It can name a juicy fruit with a thick skin that grows on a tree, or it can name a colour between red and yellow. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer has in mind.
explain: Look for clues. «She peeled an orange and shared it with her brother.» You peel fruit, not colours, so orange means the fruit here. Now read «The tiger's orange stripes seem to glow in the dark forest.» Stripes are coloured, so orange means the colour.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the meaning fits, you have it. «The orange stripes» works with the colour meaning, but «the orange stripes» as fruit would make no sense at all.
fact: Orange can be a noun for a fruit, and an adjective for a colour.
fact: An orange is a round, juicy fruit with a thick skin, and it grows on a tree.
fact: Orange is a colour between red and yellow, like carrots and pumpkins.
fact: «Orange juice» and «peel an orange» use orange as the fruit.
fact: Oranges give us vitamin C, which helps keep us healthy.
exercise: «She peeled an orange and shared it with her brother.» What is an orange in this sentence? | A loud noise | A kind of bird | A small stone | *A round, juicy fruit with a thick skin
exercise: «The tiger's orange stripes seem to glow in the dark forest.» What is orange used as here? | A fruit you can eat | A sort of tree | *A colour | A fast animal
exercise: Which sentence uses orange as a colour? | I peeled an orange. | Oranges grow on trees. | *The sky turned orange at sunset. | She bought a bag of oranges.
test: «Stars can be blue-white, yellow-white, orange or red.» What does orange mean in this sentence? | A fruit with a thick skin | *A colour between red and yellow | A loud sound | A shade of blue
test: Which word tells you where an orange grows? | Cloud | *Tree | Pond | Desk
exam: In «Juicy, round and orange, the fruit rolled off the table», what does orange describe? | *The colour of the fruit | How fast it rolled | The name of a tree | How tall the table is
